Template: indi-allsky/reuse_existing_config
Type: boolean
Default: true
Description: Reuse existing configuration and settings?
 An existing indi-allsky installation was detected.
 .
 If you select 'Yes', your existing configuration, camera drivers, web ports, admin accounts, and observatory settings will be preserved automatically.
 .
 If you select 'No', you will be guided through the interactive setup wizard to reconfigure your settings.

Template: indi-allsky/camera_interface
Type: select
Choices: indi, libcamera, simulator, test_rotating_stars, test_bubbles, indi_accumulator, indi_passive, pycurl_camera, mqtt_libcamera
Default: indi
Description: Select primary camera interface:
 Choose the camera capture subsystem for indi-allsky.
 .
  * indi: Standard INDI camera drivers (ZWO ASI, QHY, PlayerOne, ToupTek, SVBony, DSLR, etc.)
  * libcamera: Raspberry Pi native libcamera CSI subsystem (Raspi HQ Camera, Camera Module 3, etc.)
  * simulator: Simulated test camera for demonstration/testing
  * test_rotating_stars: Rotating Stars simulated sky
  * test_bubbles: Animated Bubbles simulated pattern
  * indi_accumulator: Synthetic long-exposure accumulator
  * indi_passive: Passive listener connected to existing indiserver
  * pycurl_camera: Remote HTTP camera stream downloader
  * mqtt_libcamera: Remote MQTT-controlled libcamera stream

Template: indi-allsky/libcamera_sensor
Type: select
Choices: libcamera_imx477, libcamera_imx378, libcamera_imx708, libcamera_imx519, libcamera_imx500_ai, libcamera_imx283, libcamera_imx462, libcamera_imx327, libcamera_imx678, libcamera_imx335, libcamera_ov5647, libcamera_imx219, libcamera_imx296_gs, libcamera_imx296_gs_color, libcamera_imx290, libcamera_imx298, libcamera_64mp_hawkeye, libcamera_64mp_owlsight, libcamera_generic
Default: libcamera_imx477
Description: Select libcamera sensor profile:
 Choose your specific Raspberry Pi camera sensor model for optimized gain/exposure tuning.

